estion_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">\"Ankle hold\", \"Knee hold\" are the term related to which of the following sports?</span></p>","option_1":"Basketball","option_2":"Gymnastics","option_3":"Swimming","option_4":"Kabaddi","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"4","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>Correct Answer: Option D - Kabaddi.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>'Ankle hold' and 'Knee hold' are specific tackling techniques used by defenders (the 'anti' side) in Kabaddi to catch and hold the raider by their ankle or knee, preventing them from returning to their own half and thereby scoring a point for the defending team.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29590","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"768","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">FX-CLEAR, a forex dealing system, which was launched by Clearcorp on August 7, _____.</span></p>","option_1":"2003","option_2":"2005","option_3":"2007","option_4":"2009","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - 2003.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>FX-CLEAR is an electronic trading platform for the foreign exchange (forex) market in India, developed and launched by Clearcorp Dealing Systems (India) Ltd (a subsidiary of the Clearing Corporation of India) on 7 August 2003, to facilitate transparent, real-time forex dealing among banks and financial institutions. This question was left unanswered by the candidate.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29591","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"768","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Where is the 'Thousand Pillar' Temple located?</span></p>","option_1":"Punjab","option_2":"Kerala","option_3":"Gujarat","option_4":"Telangana","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"4","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>Correct Answer: Option D - Telangana.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>The Thousand Pillar Temple (Rudreshwara Swamy Temple) is located in Warangal, Telangana, built during the Kakatiya dynasty in the 12th century. It is renowned for its intricate carvings and star-shaped architectural design, dedicated to Lord Shiva, Vishnu, and Surya.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29592","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"768","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Where is the tomb of Sher Shah Suri located?</span></p>","option_1":"Sikandra","option_2":"Sasaram","option_3":"Lahore","option_4":"Aurangabad","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Sasaram.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>The tomb of Sher Shah Suri, founder of the Suri dynasty, is located in Sasaram, Bihar, standing in the middle of an artificial lake. It is considered an important precursor to later Mughal mausoleum architecture, including the Humayun's Tomb and the Taj Mahal.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29593","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"768","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">In a compound like water, the mass ratio of hydrogen to oxygen is always _____.</span></p>","option_1":"1:14","option_2":"1:8","option_3":"1:2","option_4":"8:1","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - 1:8.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>Water (H2O) is composed of 2 hydrogen atoms (atomic mass 1 each, total 2) and 1 oxygen atom (atomic mass 16). This gives a mass ratio of hydrogen to oxygen of 2:16, which simplifies to 1:8 - a fixed ratio consistent with the Law of Constant Proportions, which states that a chemical compound always contains the same elements in the same fixed proportion by mass.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29594","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"768","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Dmitri Mendeleev was unable to assign the correct position to which element?</span></p>","option_1":"Helium","option_2":"Hydrogen","option_3":"Oxygen","option_4":"Chlorine","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Hydrogen.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>Hydrogen posed a classification problem in Mendeleev's periodic table because it exhibits properties resembling both alkali metals (Group 1, forming +1 ions) and halogens (Group 17, forming -1 ions), making it difficult to assign it a single definitive position. This anomaly remains a recognised limitation of the periodic table even in its modern form.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29595","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"768","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">M.S. Subbulakshmi is the first _____ with the Bharat Ratna in 1998.</span></p>","option_1":"musicians","option_2":"sportsperson","option_3":"painter","option_4":"author","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - musicians.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt;background-color:#ffffff\"><span>M.S. Subbulakshmi, the legendary Carnatic vocalist, was the first musician to be honoured with India's highest civilian award, the Bharat Ratna, which she received in 1998, recognising her extraordinary contribution to Indian classical music.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""}]